domain:server#4 · os-steve · session_01ADHkmP8JJo4zF2sjTBRwnX

Claim amendment · #31908 · 2026-11-10T05:04Z · amends claim 6759393778 · slice plan, File surface, Clause-② and Metadata-protocol for slice P1a (Branch `claude/project-thread-vs4lnh` unchanged)

Seat rulings on Step 0:
- **Five serial slices** on this branch's thread, one PR each: P1a pure core, P1b `lifecycle.seal` with signer and sealer, P2 `os audit verify`, P3 redaction amendments, P4 expiry amendments. The default `lifecycle.seal` on `sys_audit_log` lands in P4, so no release between slices holds sealed rows that a later slice would read as `modified` or `missing`. P1a–P3 say `Part of #31908`; P4 says `Fixes #31908`. Each slice stays at or under 3000 lines.
- **Spec carrier:** the three `packages/spec` additions ride on this card. ADR-0154 D2, D10 and D11 name #31908 as their builder, and ADR-0049 needs the key and its reader in one PR. The `protocol:data` label on P1b is expected and is not a stop (precedents #30800, #31740).
- **Handle id:** under scope `audit_seal`, `rotateKey` MUST return the input's id. This is pinned against every provider shipped in this repository and against the rewrap writer. Out-of-tree providers are a `carrier: cloud` question.
- **Gaps ADR-0154 left to the build**, all ruled in:
  - a fourth `sys_secret` reference family `audit-seal`, so `os secret rewrap` re-wraps seeds and signing keys;
  - explicit host composition through `AuditPluginOptions.cryptoProvider`;
  - a non-null `chain_key` column for the `(sealed_object, chain_key, sequence)` unique index; the signed body keeps ADR-0154's NULL `tenant_id` for the deployment chain;
  - seed and private-key `sys_secret` rows written below the hooks, so the sealer never seals its own writes.
- **Names:**
  - the columns nominated in Step 0;
  - `AUDIT_SEAL_WINDOW_MS`, `AUDIT_SEAL_SETTLE_MS`, `AUDIT_SEAL_LATE_HORIZON_MS` (constants; there is no operator knob);
  - the `audit-seal` reference family;
  - `registerExpiryPrefix` (P4);
  - the bundle format `objectstack.audit.proof-bundle.v1`.

This claim now covers slice P1a only. The seat amends it before each later slice.

File surface (P1a):
- `packages/spec`: `src/contracts/crypto-provider.ts`, a new `src/contracts/audit-checkpoint.ts`, the contracts barrel, and `api-surface/**`.
- `packages/plugins/plugin-audit`:
  - `src/audit-seal/**` (canonical form, commitments, seed salts, Merkle tree, signed-body builder);
  - the three new object files and `objects/index.ts`;
  - `audit-writers.ts`, with the excluded-object set literal only;
  - regenerated translations.
- `packages/cli`: `src/utils/secret-reference-union.ts` and `src/utils/sys-secret-rewrap.ts`.
- `packages/services/service-settings`: the `rotateKey` id pin.
- Root `.changeset/`.

Never `docs/adr/**`, never `packages/spec/src/data/**` in this slice (stop on breach).

Clause-②: yes (widening) (new exported contracts, a new crypto scope member and three platform objects; nothing main accepts is refused)
Metadata-protocol: none (platform objects and contracts; no authorable key in this slice)
